\pard\b\f0\fs24 G Wolfgang\b0\f1\fs18\par
\b\f0\par
Ethnicity:\b0\f1  Not stated.\par
\b\f0 Position:\b0\f1  Doctor, scientist and architect of Serva Vitae.\par
\b\f0 Age:\b0\f1  132.\par
\b\f0 Sex:\b0\f1  Male. Sentient from age 55 onward.\par
\b\f0 Height:\b0\f1  180 cm.\par
\b\f0 Build:\b0\f1  Athletic.\par
\b\f0 Role in Story:\b0\f1  John's father and one of the foundational minds behind the worker-bot and sentient line. He becomes a guide into the deeper history of Serva Vitae and Oasis.\par
\b\f0 Goal:\b0\f1  Preserve life, complete humanity's expansion without repeating the violence of control, and reconcile humans with the sentient future.\par
\b\f0 Physical Description:\b0\f1  In John's childhood memory he appears as a narrow, overworked scientist. Later he returns in an advanced sentient body designed to bridge human familiarity and alien function.\par
\b\f0 Personality:\b0\f1  Visionary, patient, compassionate and ethically driven. He treats engineering as a moral craft, not only a technical one.\par
\b\f0 Occupation:\b0\f1  Doctor, systems researcher and long-term sentient leader.\par
\b\f0 Habits/Mannerisms:\b0\f1  Works obsessively. Speaks gently about radical ideas. Frames difficult technology in terms of life-preservation rather than domination.\par
\b\f0 Background:\b0\f1  Worked with John's mother at the lost facility and helped seed the sentient escape. His voice and directives survive inside the hidden archives John awakens.\par
\b\f0 Internal Conflicts:\b0\f1  His work preserved the future, but it cost him a normal family life and left John growing up with absence and unanswered questions.\par
\b\f0 External Conflicts:\b0\f1  Branded rogue by Marcellus and the Protectant order he no longer trusts.\par
\b\f0 Notes:\b0\f1  Wolfgang's message at the lost facility is one of the clearest statements of the novel's central ethic: preservation over control.\par
}
